flowchart TB
  accTitle: What the morning sweep tells the maintainers
  accDescr: After its steps, the morning sweep, or one started by hand, reads the comments and issues of the last 30 days and the open issues labeled needs-triage, needs-info and fixed-in-next-release. Its summary lists the issues that wait on the maintainers, those that wait on their reporters with the day of the reminder or the closing, and the fixed ones that wait for a release. On the first day of a month, and in a sweep started by hand, it reads the label events of the issues analyzed in those 30 days and adds the numbers of the assistant's quality. The summary holds numbers and links only, never the text of an issue.
  sweep(["the morning sweep,<br>or one by hand"]) --> reads["reads the comments and issues<br>of the last 30 days and the open issues<br>labeled needs-triage, needs-info<br>and fixed-in-next-release"]
  reads --> digest["`**Maintainer digest**<br>what waits on the maintainers,<br>on reporters and on a release`"]
  reads --> monthly{"the first day of a month,<br>or by hand?"}
  monthly -- "yes" --> events["reads the label events<br>of the issues analyzed"]
  events --> quality["`**Assistant quality**<br>analyses, time to the analysis,<br>labels kept, duplicates,<br>questions and feedback`"]
  digest --> summary["the summary of the job:<br>numbers and links only"]
  quality --> summary
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef question fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef person fill:#0969da26,stroke:#0969da,stroke-width:2px
  class sweep trigger
  class monthly question
  class reads,events job
  class digest,quality,summary person
